WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.000
Good morning, I'm Josh Welsh, President of&nbsp;
Film Independent. Welcome to the 2022 Spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.280
Awards Emerging Filmmakers Awards reveal.&nbsp;
Joining me today are a three very talented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:21.440
previous Spirit Award grant winners: Ekwa Msangi,&nbsp;
Elegance Bratton and Gerry Kim. Today we will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.120
be announcing the nominees and winners of three&nbsp;
emerging filmmaker awards, the Someone To Watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.000
Producers and Truer Than Fiction awards, each&nbsp;
chosen for their unique vision and commitment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.120
to the craft. I am thrilled to say that all three&nbsp;
award winners will receive a twenty five thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.120
dollar unrestricted cash grant. Now, on with&nbsp;
the announcements... Hello I'm Ekwa Msangi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:50.160
the recipient of the 2021 Someone To Watch award&nbsp;
for my film Farewell Amour. I remember distinctly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.160
winning this award last year sitting in my kitchen&nbsp;
and feeling so overwhelmed and surprised that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:03.280
I had actually been seen and heard in what seemed&nbsp;
like a vacuous pit in the year of 2020/2021&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:11.360
with covid and being on zoom and just not&nbsp;
knowing if anyone had even seen or heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:17.920
the work that me and my team did together. So it&nbsp;
was such an honor and a pleasure and I hope that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.960
it is the same for this year's winner and leads&nbsp;
you along a wonderful path as it did for myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:31.600
and my team. I'm delighted to be announcing the&nbsp;
2022 Someone to Watch award. This is an award that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.600
honors a talented filmmaker of singular vision&nbsp;
who has not yet received appropriate recognition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.760
The finalists for this year are&nbsp;
Alex Camilleri, director of Luzzu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.840
Gillian Wallace Horvat director of&nbsp;
I Blame Society, Michael Sarnoski&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.880
director of Pig All three nominees for the Someone&nbsp;
to Watch award built distinctive worlds and filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:05.520
them with thoughtfully crafted characters and&nbsp;
stories. The winner of this year's award embraced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:11.920
the rituals of a traditional way of life as it's&nbsp;
threatened by the bureaucracies of the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.440
This director brilliantly captures the complexity&nbsp;
that exists in a seemingly simple world channeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:28.240
authenticity at every level the summon to watch&nbsp;
award goes to Alex Camilleri director of Luzzu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.920
Congratulations Alex! Hey everyone I'm Gerry&nbsp;
Kim the recipient of the 2021 Producers Award.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.240
It was an incredible honor to have received this&nbsp;
award last year since so many of its previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.120
winners went to producers I deeply deeply admire&nbsp;
and respect. I remember when it was announced last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.000
year, I was sitting in my car on a scout and&nbsp;
in complete shock that I had won and more so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.920
I was incredibly happy to have been representing&nbsp;
all the filmmakers that I previously worked with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.120
in the past and I was excited to share this&nbsp;
award with them. The Producers award honors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.960
emerging producers who despite highly limited&nbsp;
resources demonstrate the creativity tenacity and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:09.360
vision required to produce quality independent&nbsp;
films. The finalists are: Brad Becker-Parton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:18.640
Pin-Chun Liu, and Lizzie Shapiro The Producers&nbsp;
Award committee tasks themselves with selecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.680
three producers who are making high quality&nbsp;
work oftentimes with very limited means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.600
and are creating and providing opportunities for&nbsp;
emerging filmmakers from disparate backgrounds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.800
The committee has chosen to honor a producer who&nbsp;
is well respected by peers is already carving a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.720
path that reflects a commitment to films that&nbsp;
in their own words bring joy and ask complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:45.840
questions. This year's producer's award goes&nbsp;
to Lizzie Shapiro. Congratulations, Lizzy!

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:55.680
Is that your life? Yeah yes. That's my life.&nbsp;
Well, lucky you. Hi I'm Elegance Bratton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.160
the recipient of the 2021 Truer Than&nbsp;
Fiction award for my documentary Pier Kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.880
and first of all I want to say thank you&nbsp;
again the film independent and wonderful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:10.000
sponsors who made this possible. The past year&nbsp;
has been incredible our movie appeared on POV,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.320
we're currently nominated for a GLAAD award&nbsp;
and the Truer Than Fiction award has just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.560
made it possible for me to live my life as an&nbsp;
artist while also being passionate about what I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:24.160
believe in. The Truer Than Fiction award honors&nbsp;
an emerging director of nonfiction features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.040
who work has not yet received appropriate&nbsp;
recognition. This year's finalists are:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:37.840
Jessica Beshir director of Faya Dayi, Angelo&nbsp;
Madsen Minax director of North by Current,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.920
and Debbie Lum director of Try&nbsp;
Harder! Even though each are still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.240
in the beginning stages of their careers, the&nbsp;
three nominees for the truth of fiction award&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.040
helm documentaries that exemplify the range of&nbsp;
what's possible within nonfiction storytelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.840
offering deep insight to lives and situations with&nbsp;
clearly honed perspectives. The winner of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:05.920
year's award crafted a memorably contemplative&nbsp;
intimate and immersive look at the ritual and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.680
community at the complex intersection of religious&nbsp;
meditation in a lucrative national windfall.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:19.520
Without further adieu, the Truer Than Fiction&nbsp;
award goes to Jessica Beshir for Faya Deyi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.640
Congratulations Jessica! Enjoy it! Buy me a&nbsp;
drink when we see each other in real life!

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.440
And there you have it. I encourage you&nbsp;
to check out the work of our emerging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.600
filmmaker award nominees and winners&nbsp;
and extend another thank you to Ekwa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.240
Elegence and Gerry for joining us for today's&nbsp;
announcement. A special thanks to all those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:48.800
supporters of the 2022 Film Independent Spirit&nbsp;
Awards, including our Premier sponsor IFC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.400
our official spirit Bulleit Frontier Whiskey&nbsp;
and Seedlip, our official water Fiji Water and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.240
our official beer Stella Artois. Don't forget&nbsp;
to watch the Spirit Awards on Sunday, March 6th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:07.520
live on IFC at 5 pm Eastern. For more information&nbsp;
go to spiritawards.com. Congratulations to all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:19.840
emerging filmmaker award winners and nominees of&nbsp;
the 2022 Film Independent Spirit Awards. Cheers!

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:31.520
you

